                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "ROUTINE: an ongoing cycle of natural actions and patterns. WOW. This game was fucking incredible. The sound design, atmosphere, no hand holding (literally throwing you into the game with no hud, no objective icon, no information, just letting the player figure out what to do) that is how a horror game should be done. This game was so good it delivered on every front. I seriously have no complaints about this game it's scary, spooky, has actual good buildup and tension. The game really makes you feel like you're the guy you're playing as and it works perfectly. I couldn't recommend this game enough it is genuinely 1 of the greatest games I've ever played. I seriously can't think of a lot of games that can match this games atmosphere. 1 of a kind experience and I'd rate this game a 10/10. It may not be everyone's cup of tea but man if you like games that have some seriously good scares, insane detail, atmosphere for days, sound design that can send shivers down your spine, and kick ass games that don't think you're retarded and can't figure stuff out this game is perfect for you. Go into this completely blind as it was intended to be played like that. I got this game with a bundle and completely forgot about it in my library for about a year and figured I'd give it a shot and I was not disappointed in the slightest. It has really deep messaging about things I refuse to spoil in this review. Plz do yourself the favor of playing this game it is truly 1 of the best games I've ever played I haven't been this immersed in a game in a very long time.",
